process-group-private.m's worker on the machine's GPU (docs/INPROGRESS.md,
GPU processes that run loops, (s5)): each tile's group-private array is in
its team's local memory, and the one of 20000 ints, which does not fit, in
the process's memory instead.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fopenmp-version=61 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-group-private.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env %t | FileCheck %S/process-group-private.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

Under fallback(abort), the arrays that fit are made in local memory, which
5000 ints does, and the one that does not ends the program, naming the
sizes. The launch gives each team the most local memory that keeps the
kernel's team count, so the size left depends on the kernel.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fopenmp-version=61 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/process_group_private_abort.m -o %t.abort
RUN: not %gpu-env %t.abort 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ABORT
ABORT: 5000: 16357229125000
ABORT-NEXT: Merkurius runtime: a group-private array of 160008 bytes does not fit in the {{[0-9]+}} bytes of local memory left to its team, and its fallback is abort
